            <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> April 24, 2026</p>

            <h3>Overview</h3>
            <p>This Privacy Policy applies to the ResellerBooks application ("Application"). ResellerBooks is a record-keeping tool for resellers. The Application is designed to help you organize and review business records that you enter, import, or choose to sync.</p>

            <h3>Information We Collect and Use</h3>
            <p>ResellerBooks is designed so that your records remain on your device or in your personal iCloud storage unless you choose to export them or send them elsewhere.</p>
            <p>The Application may process the following information that you provide or import:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Sales and order data</li>
                <li>Expense records</li>
                <li>Mileage and trip logs</li>
                <li>Inventory and other bookkeeping details</li>
                <li>Home office and similar bookkeeping settings</li>
                <li>Photos you attach to receipts, odometer readings, or mileage logs</li>
                <li>Data imported from third-party platforms, CSV files, or API connections</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We use this information only to provide the Application’s record-keeping features. We do not sell your data.</p>

            <h3>Local Storage and iCloud Sync</h3>
            <p>The Application stores data on your device using Apple’s local storage frameworks and may optionally sync data through your private iCloud/CloudKit container if you enable iCloud on your Apple device.</p>
            <p>If iCloud sync is available, your data may be transferred through Apple’s iCloud services so that it can be available on your other devices signed into the same Apple Account. If iCloud is unavailable or disabled, your data remains local to the device.</p>
            <p>The Service Provider does not operate a separate cloud database for your records.</p>

            <h3>Photos and On-Device Processing</h3>
            <p>The Application may use on-device processing to extract text from receipt photos, odometer photos, or similar images you add to the Application.</p>
            <p>When you capture or import photos:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>The photo is stored locally and may also sync through your private iCloud storage if enabled</li>
                <li>Text extraction is performed to support record-keeping features</li>
                <li>Photos and extracted text are not intended to be sent for human review unless you choose to share or export them</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The Application requests camera access so you can scan receipts or capture mileage-related images, and photo library access so you can attach existing images to records.</p>

            <h3>Location and Mileage Features</h3>
            <p>The Application may use address lookup and route calculation services to help estimate mileage or support trip logging.</p>
            <p>If you use these features:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Address strings you enter may be sent to Apple services for geocoding or route estimation</li>
                <li>The Application does not use background GPS tracking</li>
                <li>The Application does not continuously monitor your location</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Third-Party Integrations</h3>
            <p>The Application may connect to third-party services only when you choose to use those features.</p>
            
            <h4>eBay Integration</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>If you connect your eBay account, the Application uses OAuth 2.0 authentication</li>
                <li>Your eBay password is not collected by the Application</li>
                <li>A secure authorization flow is used to obtain access to your eBay data</li>
                <li>The Application may use a secure intermediary service only to exchange the authorization code for access tokens</li>
                <li>Access tokens may be stored in the device Keychain for sign-in purposes</li>
                <li>The Application may retrieve sales and fee data from eBay when you connect your account</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>Apple Services</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>iCloud/CloudKit may be used for optional sync and backup</li>
                <li>StoreKit may be used for subscriptions and billing</li>
                <li>MapKit may be used for address lookup and route estimation</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Subscriptions and Billing</h3>
            <p>If you purchase ResellerBooks Pro, billing is handled by Apple through the App Store. The Service Provider does not receive, store, or process your payment card information.</p>

            <h3>Export Features</h3>
            <p>The Application may generate export files that include your record-keeping data and related photos. Exports are created temporarily on your device and are shared only through the method you choose, such as the iOS share sheet, email, or cloud storage.</p>

            <h3>Advertising and Analytics</h3>
            <p>The Application does not currently use third-party advertising networks, analytics providers, or behavioral tracking tools.</p>

            <h3>Data Retention and Deletion</h3>
            <p>You control your records.</p>
            <p>You may:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Delete individual entries inside the Application</li>
                <li>Disconnect third-party integrations such as eBay</li>
                <li>Delete all Application data using the Settings option provided in the app</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Deleting the Application from your device removes local data, but it may not remove copies stored in your private iCloud account. To remove iCloud-stored data, you must also delete it from your iCloud storage settings.</p>
            <p>Deleted data may not be recoverable.</p>

            <h3>Children’s Privacy</h3>
            <p>The Application is intended for adult users. It is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

            <h3>Security</h3>
            <p>We use reasonable safeguards designed to protect your information, including:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Apple device and storage protections</li>
                <li>Keychain storage for sensitive credentials</li>
                <li>Encrypted network connections where supported by the relevant service</li>
            </ul>
            <p>No method of storage or transmission is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

